92186549018 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549018 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ shown above. Which of the following is a basis of the eigenspace corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =7?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549018 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7b9e6797-8ad6-50af-aa3b-75e9f9aa6e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549018 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =7.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}0=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 8 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}.$ So, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required basis is\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549087 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549087 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ad2b66f-c218-5745-9878-11331d3e9cab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549087 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549127 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95da3e94-779f-5413-a325-1e56abe1dbec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549127 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186432015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549132 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549132 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a646c6d2-ebc3-59d4-84e2-5a1b718c10ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549132 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549146 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549146 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d601707f-3fdc-5047-9b04-055887e649a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549146 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186549018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549156 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186549146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549156 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa858142-a712-54c2-946c-6b7b0fe5ba70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186549156 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360694 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
